Z||000000||Mach10||11-13-2001||07:30 PM||||I've run a few searches, but haven't turned up too much.. Are there any other GM cars that share the EGR solenoid? Mine's getting flaky. ECM spitting codes, EGR Valve is brand-new, and working, and EGR tube is still intact (!!!). Vacuum lines are cool, so the only thing left is the EGR solley  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Don't feel like being sodomized at the parts-counter, and being that there aren't very many Fieros in our crap (sorry, Scrap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) yards, I'm wondering if anything else will work. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Two88GTs||11-13-2001||07:37 PM||||Many cars use the same basic components(3rd Gen Camaro/Firebird) but the bracket holds the solenoid+filter is different.  I think you can swap out the bracket from your old one though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||11-13-2001||07:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Two88GTs:<BR><B>Many cars use the same basic components(3rd Gen Camaro/Firebird) but the bracket holds the solenoid+filter is different.  I think you can swap out the bracket from your old one though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Don't mind that... So basically any GM 86-88 2.8L car... Just different brackets?<P>Don't mind doing that.<P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||ka4nkf||11-13-2001||08:52 PM||||You can go to <A HREF="http://www.acdelco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.acdelco.com</A>  and put the part number in and it will tell you if any other cars uses this number||||reg||1
